{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BJy246hGQi6iQKdSWzjKcr","type":"tool_result","content":"exit=0\n# Running tests in chromium\n# create a button\n# inner button uses native role and disabled semantics\n# disabled property reflects to host attribute\n# disabled property uses only native disabled state\n# autofocus property reflects to host attribute\n# setAttribute disabled still works (no loop)\n# disabled host attribute uses only native disabled state\n# preact: render button with disabled attribute\n# preact: render button without disabled attribute\n# default-rendered button has no aria-live attribute\n# inner button class attribute has no duplicate tokens\n# declarative type attribute reaches inner button\n# type setter reflects to host and inner button\n# declarative type=\"button\" reaches inner button\n# setAttribute(\"type\", ...) propagates to inner button\n# value attribute is forwarded\n# form-related attributes are forwarded\n# title attribute is forwarded\n# aria-live attribute is forwarded from a declared host\n# aria-live changes on the host update the inner button\n# removing aria-live from the host removes it from the inner button\n# preact: label content updates reactively\n# ending spinning keeps a disabled host disabled\n# spinning = false on an idle disabled button keeps it disabled\n# enabling the host while spinning keeps it disabled\n# spinning preserves aria-busy updates\n# keydown does not synthesize a click\n# hydrates an inner button rendered by the app\n# hydrates aria-live onto an inner button rendered by the app\n# forwards a class added to the host to the inner button\n# moves a changed host class onto the inner button\n# keeps the element classes when the host class changes\n# updates the inner button when a Preact class prop changes\n# hydrates a host class change onto an app-rendered button\n# hydrates the first host class onto an app-rendered button\n# moves a host aria-label onto the inner button\n# moves a late host aria-label onto the inner button\n# ariaLabel property names the inner button\n# ariaLabel set before connect reaches the built button\n# preact: ariaLabel prop names the inner button\n# preact: ariaLabel applies to an app-rendered button\n# preact: ariaLabel reads the app-rendered button after a swap\n# all done\n# tests 104\n# pass  104\n# ok","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5aa86eda-6733-46a0-b6e0-9c8b01a8bd77","uuid":"8b556d36-c1d5-49ad-83f7-8fb2315ccf47","timestamp":"2026-10-30T03:30:33.538Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"exit=0\n# Running tests in chromium\n# create a button\n# inner button uses native role and disabled semantics\n# disabled property reflects to host attribute\n# disabled property uses only native disabled state\n# autofocus property reflects to host attribute\n# setAttribute disabled still works (no loop)\n# disabled host attribute uses only native disabled state\n# preact: render button with disabled attribute\n# preact: render button without disabled attribute\n# default-rendered button has no aria-live attribute\n# inner button class attribute has no duplicate tokens\n# declarative type attribute reaches inner button\n# type setter reflects to host and inner button\n# declarative type=\"button\" reaches inner button\n# setAttribute(\"type\", ...) propagates to inner button\n# value attribute is forwarded\n# form-related attributes are forwarded\n# title attribute is forwarded\n# aria-live attribute is forwarded from a declared host\n# aria-live changes on the host update the inner button\n# removing aria-live from the host removes it from the inner button\n# preact: label content updates reactively\n# ending spinning keeps a disabled host disabled\n# spinning = false on an idle disabled button keeps it disabled\n# enabling the host while spinning keeps it disabled\n# spinning preserves aria-busy updates\n# keydown does not synthesize a click\n# hydrates an inner button rendered by the