{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgXiWKDfm6JMt3ct8empV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PHY77UeVqmrcHtNczkrsZA","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='AGENTS.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nold=\"inspect inner-button attributes through `el.button` rather than rendered HTML.\\n\"\nnew=old+(\"`tapout` always listens on port 8123, so a run fails with `EADDRINUSE`\\n\"\n\"while another worktree's suite is running. Wait for the port to free and\\n\"\n\"rerun; do not kill the other process.\\n\")\nassert old in s\nopen(p,'w').write(s.replace(old,new))\nEOF\ncat > .nightralph/notes.md <<'EOF'\n# 01-verify-class-following notes\n\n## Outcome\nImplementation in src/client.ts already matched every class decision in the\nspec (OWNED_CLASSES export, diff-based handleChange_class that no-ops with\nno button, spinning toggle is a no-op via owned skip, connectedCallback\nre-applies host class after hydration, `class` observed and not in\nFORWARDED_ATTRS, `class` in HANDLED_KEYS in src/html.ts). No source changes.\n\n## How I verified\nRan the suite (green), then mutation-tested src/client.ts:\n- handleChange_class made a no-op -> 7 class assertions fail\n- owned skip removed from the remove loop -> \"keeps spinning\" fails\n- connectedCallback re-apply removed -> first-host-class hydration fails\n- owned skip removed from the add loop -> NOTHING failed (gap)\n\n## Changes (test/index.ts only)\n1. New test \"a host class change never adds an element class\": a\n   non-spinning host whose class becomes \"spinning other\" must not put\n   `spinning` on el.button. Fails under the add-loop mutation, passes on\n   the real code. (Code was already correct, so \"red\" was demonstrated\n   against the mutation.)\n2. The three Preact class tests read the inner button through\n   `el.button` instead of `container.querySelector('button')`, matching\n   the ticket wording and AGENTS.md.\n\n## Reading of criteria\nChecklist items 1-6 were already covered by existing tests; I treated\n\"verify\" as \"prove the tests fail when the behavior breaks\".\n\n## Environment gotcha\ntapout binds port 8123; another worktree held it, giving EADDRINUSE. I\nwaited for the port instead of killing the process. Recorded in AGENTS.md.\nEOF\ngit add AGENTS.md && git commit -q -m \"docs: note tapout port collisions across worktrees\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\"; git status --short"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":305,"cache_read_input_tokens":62957,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":305},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5aa86eda-6733-46a0-b6e0-9c8b01a8bd77","uuid":"7f651c67-fe26-4d4b-ade7-6dd7d7bf5a6f","timestamp":"2026-10-30T03:32:11.040Z","request_id":"req_011CgXiWJvJA8K8gT4bCumCD","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01PHY77UeVqmrcHtNczkrsZA":{"command":"cd /Users/nick/code/button.forward-class-and-aria-label-01-verify-class-following && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='AGENTS.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nold=\"inspect inner-button attributes through `el.button` rather than rendered HTML.\\n\"\nnew=old+(\"`tapout` always listens on port 8123, so a run fails with `EADDRINUSE`\\n\"\n\"while another worktree's suite is running. Wait for the port to free and\\n\"\n\"rerun; do not kill the other process.\\n\")\nassert old in s\nopen(p,'w').write(s.replace(old,new))\nEOF\ncat > .nightralph/notes.md <<'EOF'\n# 01-verify-class-following notes\n\n## Outcome\nImplementation in src/client.ts already matched every class decision in the\nspec (OWNED_CLASSES export, diff-based handleChange_class that no-ops with\nno button, spinning toggle is a no-op via owned skip, connectedCallback\nre-applies host class after hydration, `class` observed and not in\nFORWARDED_ATTRS, `class` in HANDLED_KEYS in src/html.ts). No source changes.\n\n## How I verified\nRan the suite (green), then mutation-tested src/client.ts:\n- handleChange_class made a no-op -> 7 class assertions fail\n- owned skip removed from the remove loop -> \"keeps spinning\" fails\n- connectedCallback re-apply removed -> first-host-class hydration fails\n- owned skip removed from the add loop -> NOTHING failed (gap)\n\n## Changes (test/index.ts only)\n1. New test \"a host class change never adds an element class\": a\n   non-spinning host whose class becomes \"spinning other\" must not put\n   `spinning` on el.button. Fails under the add-loop mutation, passes on\n   the real code. (Code was already correct, so \"red\" was demonstrated\n   against the mutation.)\n2. The three Preact class tests read the inner button through\n   `el.button` instead of `container.querySelector('button')`, matching\n   the ticket wording and AGENTS.md.\n\n## Reading of criteria\nChecklist items 1-6 were already covered by existing tests; I treated\n\"verify\" as \"prove the tests fail when the behavior breaks\".\n\n## Environment gotcha\ntapout binds port 8123; another worktree held it, giving EADDRINUSE. I\nwaited for the port instead of killing the process. Recorded in AGENTS.md.\nEOF\ngit add AGENTS.md && git commit -q -m \"docs: note tapout port collisions across worktrees\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\"; git status --short"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01PHY77UeVqmrcHtNczkrsZA":{"cwd":"/Users/nick/code/button.forward-class-and-aria-label-01-verify-class-following"}}}
